cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the article below and the software itself."
type: software
title: "qrc-credit-default: code for 'Quantum Reservoir Computing for Credit Card Default Prediction on a Neutral Atom Platform'"
abstract: >-
  Quantum reservoir computing pipeline for credit-card default prediction. Tabular features are encoded
  into the Hamiltonian of a Rydberg neutral-atom array through local detunings or atom positions, evolved
  in emulation or on the QuEra Aquila analog quantum computer, and read out as single-site and two-site
  observables that serve as features for classical classifiers.
